# The stage removal: Aerochrome's row now carries Sky saturation 0 and Sky colour smoothing 0, and the existing field that stops Restore depth topping the sky up, which another look already uses. The saturation stage's second gate and the thin-structure removal are switched off for every look by two named constants, read by the screen, the export and the selection builder alike, and the sky map that Sky saturation alone used to ask for is no longer asked for. That is the plan's own shape: stages taken out of the look and left in the source, switched off, named for a later plan. No new stage, no new correction, no new look field and no new control was added; the constants are off-switches that no reader reaches. The preview-version constant moved with the picture change and its stamp was written by its tool. The diagnostic line that names the sky reference now says the gate is off when it is, which follows from the constant and adds no behaviour.
